        ("All we want is everything in real time, all the time.", "Jim's Big Ego"),
        ("[The] Yan’an [Soviet] is [a] synonym of crushing dissent, real or invented, by torturing and killing. As [Communist Party member] Cai Qi reminded the audience at the April 28 [2024] symposium, the Yan’an Rectification Campaign was plotted by Mao, but its main organizer was Ren Bishi.", "Yan'an Rectification Movement"),
        ("My tattoos symbolise something to me, after all they will remain with me forever.", "Aiysha Saagar"),
        ("The primary difference between a man and a woman is that man gets his self-esteem when a woman says yes and a women gets hers when she says no.", "Amy's Orgasm"),
        ("[a talk-show host accuses Amy of being a lesbian due to her bad opinions on men] I don't think I'm a lesbian because when I fantasize, I fantasize about sucking dick.", "Amy's Orgasm"),
        ("[When asked what she fantasizes about sexually] The thought of seducing a celibate man away from his allegiance to God.", "Amy's Orgasm"),
        ("I had a physical orgasm, but not a mental one, where you let someone inside and you really see yourself.", "Amy's Orgasm"),
        ("You have a unique talent for having bad taste in men.", "Amy's Orgasm"),
        ("Nanoha: I am the one who has been given a mission. Under the contract, release those powers unto me. Winds to the sky, stars to the heavens, and the unyielding soul to this heart! Magic to these hands! Raising Heart, set up!\nRaising Heart: Stand by, ready. Set up.", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("In this episode, Nanoha learns of the Jewel Seeds and starts trying to find and seal them.\nNanoha Takamachi: What'll you do when your powers come back?\nYuuno Scrya: I'll continue searching for the Jewel Seeds... alone.\nNanoha: I can't let you do that.", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Nanoha: The way I see it, if someone needs your help and you have the power to help them out, there shouldn't be a doubt as to what you should do.", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("A Jewel Seed causes a city-wide catastrophe in Nanoha's home of Uminari City.\nRaising Heart: Area search.\nNanoha Takamachi: Lyrical, magical! Search for the root of this terrible misfortune!", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Nanoha: Now I can seal it away!\nYuuno Scrya: It's impossible from here, you have to get closer!\nNanoha: It's all right, I can do it! We can do it, can't we, Raising Heart?\nRaising Heart: Shooting Mode. Set up.", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Even while going to a hot spring to relax, Nanoha worries about the Jewel Seeds and the mysterious girl she met.\nYuuno Scrya: Nanoha, go after the girl!\nArf: Do you really think I'd let that happen?!\nYuuno: I'll make sure it happens!", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Amidst Fate and Nanoha's continuing fight for the Jewel Seeds, a third group arrives.\nNanoha Takamachi: Wait a minute... All I want to do is talk to you for a bit, Fate. I have an idea though. I'm not some spoiled kid, so if you wanna fight, let's fight. But if I win... Will you talk to me?", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Nanoha: (silently) Someone to share my feelings... Someone with whom I can split the loneliness and sadness in half... That's it. Now I understand what I want. I want to share my feelings with this girl. (out loud to Fate) All I want... is to be friends.", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Fate and Nanoha battle for the last time.\nNanoha Takamachi: Try this one. It's a variation of my Divine Buster!\nRaising Heart: Starlight Breaker.\nNanoha: Now with greatest power! Starlight... Breaker!!", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("The Time-Space Administration, aided by Nanoha, advances to the final battle against Precia Testarossa.\nChrono Harlaown: You can choose whether or not you want to run away from reality, or you can face it head on like everyone else who's ever suffered!", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Six months after the first season, Nanoha is living peacefully when she is suddenly attacked.\nNanoha Takamachi: Lyrical, magical! Glimmers to be blessings, come into my hands. Ring and echo under the guidance. Divine Shooter... Shoot!", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Nanoha Takamachi: Listen to me...\nRaising Heart: Divine...\nNanoha: To what I have to say!\nRaising Heart: Buster.", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Fate, Nanoha, and Amy keep an eye on the Wolkenritter while the senior members of the TSAB are back at headquarters.\nAmy Limiette: Oh well, I'm sure there won't be that many emergencies going on while they're gone. (sirens sound)", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Vita: Hey you! Nano-something or other!\nNanoha Takamachi: It's me, Nanoha! Na-no-ha!", "Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"),
        ("Who can care what the season is, care what the reason is? It's a Christmas-y, it's a Christmas day!", "Heidi's Song"),
        ("Of all the sounds I'll ever hear, of all the sounds I've heard, the sound I fear that hurts my ear, the sound of an un-kind word.", "Heidi's Song"),
        ("Grandfather: Can you mend a coat or tend a goat or make a cake? Huh? Can you churn the milk until the cream ascends?\nHeidi: I can't mend a coat or tend a goat or make a cake, but I'm good at making friends.\nGrandfather: Making friends?!", "Heidi's Song"),
        ("..every day I can benefit from Mr. B [his teacher, Van de Sande Bakhuyzen ] is another profit.. ..day by day my ambition is growing. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("..it is a masterpiece [painting of Barend Cornelis Koekkoek: 'View on the Woods' 1839, with sizes 176 x 160 cm], a well-executed brave undertaking to imagine something like that on a large scale with such an elaborateness. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("I also sold some drawings [he means his watercolors] - the Dutch pieces [he painted in The Netherlands] sell rather well [in Brussels, where he lived then]. People seem to prefer colored drawings here. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("There is still some study [to do] here for the Dutch landscape, and I believe the best I can do is to stay some time longer. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("That [watercolor] with the Cows has been partially washed out [reducing colors] and that ugly hedge of willow trees has been taken out, and is already doing better, but the paper is not a good quality. I don't know I'll finish it or make a new one. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("The drawings [his watercolors] usually succeed in one day or at most two days or they develop difficult and usually don't finish well, then.. ..[I hope] the end will be as good as the beginning. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("Then make those studies outside. With the utmost simplicity you try to get rid of all the so-called manners, and try in one word to follow nature with feeling, but without thinking about the works of others. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("I hope to compensate this year [in 1866 Roelofs was seriously ill] the damage of so little studies [watercolors and drawings] once and for all because most of the old ones I already used [for his oil-paintings]. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("Bosboom seemed to have enjoyed my drawing [= watercolor] - He gave me a small visual comment - which I accepted with thanks and will follow. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("My sketch [in watercolor, made in 1861] represents the Hunebed in Tinaarlo in Drenthe, which I drew a few years ago; I have still the intention to paint it [oil-painting after, after his watercolor].. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("I will soon have finished another drawing [= watercolor], in the spirit as Den Tessaro [art-seller in Antwerp] wished another one, that is 'airy' and 'thin', with 'lots of space', etc.-. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
        ("Lately I have been asking for landscape [paintings] with animals, so I have devoted a lot of time this year sketching cows. (translation from original Dutch: Fons Heijnsbroek)", "Willem Roelofs"),
